    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0197" n="123" xml:id="pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5352</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-10T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1556. Your 1394, June 14, 5 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d172-f1"/> Navy Department
                    regrets that it cannot send division of destroyers, as suggested. The service of
                    American destroyers in British waters has enabled Great Britain to send British
                    destroyers to White Sea.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
